# Build context for the image defined by Dockerfile.
#
# This directory is ~961 MB on a development machine and the image needs ~12 MB of
# it. Without this file every `docker build` ships the virtualenv, the training
# corpora and 59 superseded model candidates to the Docker daemon before the first
# instruction runs. Render builds from a git clone, where the ignored paths are
# absent in any case, so what this file really does is make a LOCAL build behave
# like the deployed one.
#
# It is a second line of defence, not the primary one: the Dockerfile copies only
# requirements.txt, app/ and the four released artifacts, so nothing excluded here
# could reach an image layer even if this file were deleted.

# The virtualenv belongs to the host and is built for Windows; the image builds its
# own from requirements.txt.
.venv/
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo

# Secrets never enter a build context. ml-service/.env holds ML_API_KEY, which is
# configured through Render's dashboard instead. .env.example is not matched by
# either pattern and is harmless.
.env
*.env

# Training inputs, the offline pipeline and the evidence packs. None of it is read
# at serve time.
data/
reports/
training/

# Every artifact except the four the registry actually serves.
models/*
!models/*_latest.joblib

# Host-only tooling and scratch output.
run_dev.ps1
intent_errors.txt
